# Security headers + /diag-feed/ removal (M-headers + L-diag-feed, 2026-11-24):
# The public edge sent no Content-Security-Policy, X-Frame-Options or
# Permissions-Policy (HSTS, nosniff and Referrer-Policy were already present at
# server level). nginx `add_header` is NOT inherited: any location that defines
# its own add_header loses every server-level one, so the three headers go to
# the server level AND after the last add_header in every location that defines
# its own — the same rule SEC-05 (nginx-hardening.patch) used for HSTS.
# This patch adds 56 x 3 header lines: server level on the port-80 default and
# both HTTPS servers, plus 53 locations with their own add_headers (26 per HTTPS
# server, /download/ on port 80). Locations with no add_header of their own
# (/operator, /admin, ^~ /api/, /) inherit the server-level headers untouched.
# It also deletes the two temporary /diag-feed/ locations (one per HTTPS server,
# added 2026-11-13): the feed service is dead (probed 404), and the block's own
# removal comment says to delete it. The service itself must still be stopped
# live (`kill $(cat /home/ubuntu/diag-feed.pid)`) — that is a live step, not a
# patch step.
# CSP value: `default-src 'self'` with an 'unsafe-inline' carve-out for scripts
# and styles and `blob:` workers — the panel templates carry no inline scripts
# today, but the proxied code-server shell may, and a CSP that breaks the panel
# would be reverted the same day. It still blocks third-party sources and all
# framing (`frame-ancestors 'none'`, X-Frame-Options DENY). Tighten later once
# the panel's inline-script inventory is proven empty under the live shell.
# NOT touched: the Certbot port-80 redirect server (301s only, no content), and
# HSTS anywhere (SEC-05 owns it — see the interaction note below).
# SEC-05 INTERACTION: this patch anchors to the CURRENT live file (md5 below),
# the same anchor SEC-05 uses. Both patches insert after the last add_header in
# the same 28 locations, so whichever lands second must rebase its patch: if
# SEC-05 lands first, re-anchor these 28 hunks after its HSTS line; if this
# lands first, SEC-05 re-anchors the same way. The gate must verify
# `git apply --check` against the then-current file either way.
# Anchor: live /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/radd-stream, md5 73fdcff003edb79b246ac77705f27f3e,
# fetched 2026-11-24 (1,465 lines). Gate step: verify `git apply --check`
# against the then-current file, apply, `sudo nginx -t`, reload, then prove
# with `curl -sI` that /api/v2/play, /api/v2/resolve and /api/v1/stream
# responses carry Content-Security-Policy, X-Frame-Options and
# Permissions-Policy, and that /diag-feed/ answers 404 from nginx (no proxy).
